                <pb facs="0567" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg493"/>

                <head>No. 6.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center"
                            >[Telegram.—Translation.—<placeName>Madrid</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-14">February
                        14</date>—night.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">To the Consular Agent of the United States,
                    Ferrol:</hi></p>
                <p>Orders have been given not to permit the transshipment of men, ammunition, and
                    supplies from the Louisa Anna Fanny to the Stonewall, and that the latter should
                    not better her condition in these things whilst she is in Spanish waters. Watch
                    over their execution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PERRY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
